Message-ID: <BF24951D-1101-4373-ABDF-D1220FDFBA75@r-project.org>

Chances are that Apple's MRJ classes are incompatible with your Java. Try re-creating them from the MRJ stubs:

rm -rf MRJ.jar com
javac -d . -source 1.4 -target 1.4 ../util/MRJstubs/*.java
make MRJ.jar
make

Cheers,
Simon


